  "public": {
    "story": {
      "en": "Ms Lin taught maths at a county secondary school for thirty-one years. Her students remember two things: she never rushed a problem, and there was always a radio, opened up, on her office windowsill.\n\nShe used to say that mending a radio and solving a problem are the same thing: first listen carefully to what is wrong, then go one part at a time.\n\nShe applied for this plaque herself. She is very much alive, and comes back now and then to add to it.",
      "zh": "林老师在一所县城中学教了三十一年数学。学生们记得她两件事：讲题从不赶时间；办公室窗台上永远摆着一台拆开的收音机。\n\n她常说，修收音机和解题是一回事：先听清楚哪里不对，再一个零件一个零件地找。\n\n这块铭牌是她自己申请的。她身体很好，隔一阵子会回来添几句。"
    },
